    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="1045" n="1035" xml:id="pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. H. Wendell Endicott
                        to Brigadier General Bernhard A. Johnson, at
                        Shanghai</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-12">12 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84249. Refer 82715 of 30 March and 83352 of 5 April. General Marshall<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d758-f1"/> has been assured that he will be consulted
                    regarding contracts at which surplus property will be sold to China under credit
                    agreement. Desire that you secure his approval to price clause in sales contract
                    which you have been authorized to consummate with Chinese Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d758-f1" n="12" xml:id="d758-f1-content">
                <p>General Marshall was on a visit to Washington from China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
